WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:01.650
SPEAKER: Growth happens fast.

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:03.540
Since we last talked,
Critter Junction

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.280
just bought another
gaming company

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:08.010
to enable cross-platform gaming.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:10.110
Now you can raise
virtual pets with friends

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:13.777
on PC, Android, and
internet-connected calculators.

00:00:13.777 --> 00:00:15.360
Let's look at how
Critter Junction was

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:18.600
able to quickly integrate this
new company's infrastructure

00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:19.390
into their stack.

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:29.240
When Critter Junction first
bought the new company,

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.420
there was one major concern.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:34.010
They had an entirely
different Cloud provider

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.737
and a different architecture.

00:00:36.737 --> 00:00:38.570
Critter Junction switched
over to containers

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:39.680
and microservices.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.780
The new company's tech
stack was a monolith

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:43.890
taking over the entire VM.

00:00:43.890 --> 00:00:46.670
Critter Junction uses a
cloud native approach.

00:00:46.670 --> 00:00:49.710
The new company was
hosting everything on-prem.

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:52.160
Critter Junction really wanted
to acquire the new company

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.530
to add its cross-platform
functionality

00:00:54.530 --> 00:00:56.067
to its own offering.

00:00:56.067 --> 00:00:57.650
But everyone involved
thought it would

00:00:57.650 --> 00:00:59.570
take too much time
and engineering

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.790
efforts to actually integrate.

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:03.440
Luckily, Critter
Junction called us

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:05.360
before they turned
down this opportunity

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.600
to expand their offering while
still being able to scale

00:01:08.600 --> 00:01:11.330
and manage diverse systems.

00:01:11.330 --> 00:01:14.060
We told them about Google
Cloud's Anthos platform,

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:17.570
which lets you run apps
anywhere using GKE.

00:01:17.570 --> 00:01:19.820
The idea is to provide
a single platform

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:23.820
for managing all Kubernetes
workloads wherever they are,

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.880
including on-prem
and other clouds.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.670
This works because
Migrate from Anthos

00:01:28.670 --> 00:01:31.760
can turn VMs and physical
servers into a Kubernetes

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:34.940
pod, which can run
inside of a cluster just

00:01:34.940 --> 00:01:36.950
like any other pod.

00:01:36.950 --> 00:01:40.320
Once Critter Junction decided to
go ahead with this acquisition,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:43.670
they had a Google Cloud partner
solution team come on site

00:01:43.670 --> 00:01:46.790
to help them set up
a GKE on-prem cluster

00:01:46.790 --> 00:01:49.250
and migrate over their
newly acquired company's

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.900
existing infrastructure.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:54.170
Next the team helped them set
up an Anthos Service Mesh,

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:56.810
a fully managed service
mesh to handle communication

00:01:56.810 --> 00:02:00.020
between their on-prem
cluster and their current GKE

00:02:00.020 --> 00:02:03.500
cluster, which allowed the
on-prem workloads to be visible

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.780
inside of the Cloud console.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.120
From this point they could
manage all their workloads

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:11.630
in one place, enable
cluster load balancing,

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:14.090
and scale their services
beyond a single cluster

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:14.990
or environment.

00:02:14.990 --> 00:02:17.570
Originally, Critter Junction
was hesitant to acquire

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.120
a new company even though
it made business sense,

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.790
because they were afraid
of the risks and complexity

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:24.650
of managing a hybrid solution.

00:02:24.650 --> 00:02:27.710
But Anthos let Critter Junction
manage the diverse workloads

00:02:27.710 --> 00:02:30.020
they acquired from one
place without having

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:32.030
to move them to Google Cloud.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:35.390
They could migrate existing
VMs into containers,

00:02:35.390 --> 00:02:38.270
get unified traffic management,
and scale their operations

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:41.250
and take on new
business opportunities.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:43.943
So that's a wrap for this
episode of Season of Scale.

00:02:43.943 --> 00:02:46.110
Check out the link below
to learn more about Anthos,

00:02:46.110 --> 00:02:48.620
and stay tuned to
learn more about how

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:50.480
Critter Junction
continues to improve

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.455
the design of their app
architecture and dev processes.

00:02:53.455 --> 00:02:57.310
And remember, always
be architecting.

